Addresses WI-masad (INV-kahit). An lru_cache body runs once and its later callers were never paired with its statements. The recorder wraps functools.lru_cache for repository code: a body runs under its own coverage context |shared|cache|<file>::<qualname>, and every test that calls the cached function inherits its rows at the fold. Reads and child processes of a body go to the callers of that cache entry. Caches made before the recorder loaded are held back from narrowing and named. Evidence: full run 41,330 passed in 707 s (689-703 s without); 66 fixture + 22 cache contexts; never narrowed 427. Live control (_get_php_parser returns None): 12 failed, 12 selected. Mutations: 35 planted, 34 red; E4 equivalent (the cache raises the same TypeError one line later).
